<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::chokepoint_transit_cap" target="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained fall in shipping chokepoint throughput creates persistent supply insecurity for energy and goods, lifting inflation expectations and term premia and thereby pushing up long‑term sovereign yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::chokepoint_transit_cap" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Attacks or closures that reduce throughput at Middle Eastern chokepoints force rerouting, lengthen transit times and raise insurance/logistics costs, causing delays and reduced volume of weapons and heavy equipment shipments destined for Europe and Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::chokepoint_transit_cap" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::supply_chain_resilience" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Reductions in throughput at key Middle East maritime chokepoints from attacks or interdiction directly increase transit delays, route fragility and single‑point dependencies, thereby degrading the resilience of semiconductor supply networks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::chokepoint_transit_cap" target="western_alliance_realign::integration_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Reductions in chokepoint throughput (i.e., lower transit capacity) increase political pressure to create formal collective maritime security, shared logistics and preferential corridor arrangements among Western institutions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
