<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="global_bond_rate_shock::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating military intensity in the region triggers risk‑off portfolio shifts and mandate/liquidity withdrawals by global investors, producing net capital outflows from exposed countries and into safe‑haven assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="global_bond_rate_shock::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher conflict intensity raises counterparty, operational and sanction risks for market‑makers and funds, prompting inventory cuts, wider dealer spreads and reduced willingness to trade, which directly compresses bond market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_dynamics" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An intensification of kinetic operations in the Iran regional conflict draws US/NATO naval and air assets and political attention away from Europe, lowering short-term deterrence signaling and increasing opportunities and incentives for Russia to take escalatory actions in Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_str" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp escalations and high‑profile kinetic activity attributed to Iran or its proxies prompt policymakers to broaden and tighten export controls on dual‑use and advanced technologies to prevent diversion and limit adversary access.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="western_alliance_realign::diplomatic_signal_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharper and more frequent kinetic incidents prompt emergency consultations, ministerial calls, public statements and high-level visits among Western capitals to coordinate responses and deconfliction.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_regional_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="western_alliance_realign::policy_alignment_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating military activity produces a shared threat assessment that drives coordinated sanctions, arms transfers and unified diplomatic positions across Western governments.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_regional_conflict</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
