<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="global_bond_rate_shock::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased cohesion among Western allies enables coordinated sanctions, asset freezes and regulatory measures that accelerate capital flight from Russian/targeted assets and redirect net cross-border flows into core sovereign bond markets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="iran_regional_conflict::financial_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger cohesion among Western allies over the Ukraine crisis lowers uncertainty about coordinated responses in adjacent theatres, which reduces geopolitical risk spreads and thus the financial risk premium priced into markets tied to Middle East exposures.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_supply_con" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger Western alliance coordination on trade, investment screening and industrial incentives channels new fab and supplier contracts toward a smaller set of allied jurisdictions, increasing geographic concentration of advanced semiconductor production among friendly nodes and away from China.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
