<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_dynamics" target="global_bond_rate_shock::short_term_policy_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Marked escalation episodes disrupt energy/commodity supplies and lift near-term inflation expectations, prompting monetary authorities to raise short-term policy rates to counter rising inflation risks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_dynamics" target="iran_regional_conflict::conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp escalation in Ukraine ties down diplomatic and military attention and creates perceived windows of opportunity that Iranian leadership and proxy groups exploit to increase kinetic operations in the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_dynamics" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_str" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A rapid uptick in escalation creates emergency risk assessments and legal/political cover for the U.S. and partners to broaden and accelerate export-control lists and enforcement (covering dual‑use and semiconductor-related items), tightening flows relevant to the US–China tech competition within weeks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_dynamics" target="western_alliance_realign::integration_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Episodes of cross-border strikes, use of new weapon types or rapid tit-for-tat reprisals increase perceived collective risk among allies and generate political momentum to accelerate institutional measures (force posture changes, interoperability programs, collective planning).</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
