<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_str" target="global_bond_rate_shock::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter export controls raise compliance costs and legal/market uncertainty for foreign investors and trading partners, prompting rapid pullbacks of portfolio and trade-related financing and reducing net cross-border capital flows into affected sectors and jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_str" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">When the US tightens export controls in the tech rivalry with China, allied governments rapidly harmonize restrictions, compliance rules and secondary‑sanctions policies to protect markets and supply chains, producing more aligned decision‑making and coordinated economic/security responses.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::export_control_str" target="western_alliance_realign::policy_alignment_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">When the U.S. tightens export controls, allied governments are pressured to adopt comparable licensing rules and secondary‑sanctions‑aware restrictions to preserve market access and legal interoperability, raising cross‑jurisdiction policy alignment.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
