<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::short_term_policy_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher short-term policy rates raise borrowing and rollover costs for donor governments and defence contractors, tightening fiscal space and delaying or scaling back procurement and payments that fund weapons deliveries to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::short_term_policy_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::capital_invest_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Hikes in short-term policy rates increase bank lending costs and corporate borrowing rates for working capital and project loans, prompting firms to delay or cancel near-term capex in semiconductor and related manufacturing.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::short_term_policy_rate" target="western_alliance_realign::integration_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An abrupt increase in global short-term policy rates raises near‑term borrowing costs and recession risk, prompting governments to defer politically and fiscally costly integration measures (new pooled funds, membership expansions) and thereby lowering institutional integration pressure.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="global_bond_rate_shock::yield_curve_slope" id="0">
