<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="iran_regional_conflict::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in long-term sovereign yields typically strengthens the dollar and raises global discount rates, reducing non‑USD demand and near‑term demand expectations for crude and thereby exerting downward pressure on dollar‑priced oil.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_cap_balance" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in long-term sovereign yields increases government debt-servicing burdens and the long-run cost of financing major procurements, slowing modernization and force generation among Western backers and thereby eroding their cumulative capability advantage relative to Russia.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::capital_invest_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Persistent increases in long-term sovereign yields raise discount rates and expected financing costs for multi-year fabs, lowering NPV and leading firms to scale back or postpone investment in tech manufacturing capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rate_shock::long_term_yield" target="western_alliance_realign::policy_alignment_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in long-term sovereign yields increases government debt-servicing costs and crowding‑out risk, forcing administrations to prioritize domestic fiscal consolidation and diverge on costly foreign policy commitments, reducing cross-jurisdictional policy alignment.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d40">western_alliance_realign</data>
</edge>
