  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Institutional integration pressure facilitates coordinated maritime enforcement (escorts, embargo enforcement, temporary closures) to implement collective measures, which can temporarily reduce throughput through narrow sea chokepoints like the Strait of Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="western_alliance_realign::integration_pressure" target="iran_regional_conflict::financial_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Greater pressure toward formal integration enables synchronized sanctions, secondary measures and regulatory alignments that raise counterparty and sovereign risk perceptions, lifting spreads, insurance costs and other geopolitical risk premia for the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_regional_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="western_alliance_realign::integration_pressure" target="russia_ukraine_war::weapons_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Institutional integration pressure creates fast-track agreement mechanisms and standing procedures (e.g., mutual-assistance clauses and harmonized export approvals) that directly accelerate and increase cross-border weapons deliveries into Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="western_alliance_realign::integration_pressure" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::capital_invest_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger institutional pressure for integration drives joint subsidy schemes, pooled procurement commitments and regulatory harmonisation that make investment in allied tech manufacturing projects comparatively more attractive, redirecting private and public capital into those builds.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">western_alliance_realign</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
